ocial media’s impact in the engagement-optimized mass-platform era has been more detrimental than beneficial: its connection, knowledge and opportunity gains are substantial but often substitutable, targetable and reversible, whereas violence, youth developmental injury, privacy loss and institutional distrust are more unevenly imposed, persistent and sometimes irreversible. \nInformation, democracy and public safety receives the greatest weight because it has the broadest spillovers—corrupted information weakens health, markets, relationships and regulation simultaneously—and Myanmar demonstrates that platform failure can convert communication advantages into physical persecution, making this domain’s severe downside outweigh the other domains’ net benefits. [shard_03406_3576] [shard_00992_13016] [shard_05518_79195]", "documents": 40, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4654, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 2275}}
